CAT = "cpaiscSocReport"; SEG = "SRP"
Q = [
("What does a type 2 service auditor's report include that a type 1 report does not?",
 "Tests of controls and results", ["Management's written assertion", "Description of the system", "Opinion on control design"],
 "A type 2 report adds an opinion on operating effectiveness over the period and a description of the tests of controls and results. Both types include the description, assertion and design opinion."),
("The alert in a SOC 1 type 2 report restricts its use to:",
 "Management, users and their auditors", ["The service organization's board only", "Any party holding a contract", "Investors and lenders"],
 "AT-C 320 requires the alert to limit use to management of the service organization, user entities during the period, and the auditors of their financial statements or ICFR."),
("A service auditor finds deviations in a control but concludes its control objective was still achieved. In the description of tests and results, the deviations are:",
 "Still described with their extent", ["Left out as immaterial", "Reported only to management", "Grounds for a qualified opinion"],
 "AT-C 320 requires the number and nature of deviations even if the objective was achieved, because a deviation may matter to a particular user entity. Materiality is not applied to that disclosure."),
("Which situation requires the service auditor to modify the opinion in a SOC 1 report?",
 "Controls not suitably designed", ["CUECs noted in the description", "Use of the carve-out method", "Deviations within the expected rate"],
 "A modified opinion is required when the description is not fairly presented, controls are not suitably designed or did not operate effectively, or evidence is insufficient. The carve-out method is a normal presentation choice."),
("When a service auditor disclaims an opinion, the report should not:",
 "Describe the procedures performed", ["Give the reasons for the disclaimer", "Identify findings already found", "Identify the service organization"],
 "AT-C 320 says a disclaimer should not describe the procedures performed or the engagement's characteristics, which might overshadow it. Findings already reached are still identified."),
("Service organization management refuses to provide the written representations AT-C 320 requires. This refusal is:",
 "A scope limitation", ["Grounds only for an adverse opinion", "Acceptable if evidence suffices", "A subsequent event"],
 "AT-C 320 says refusal constitutes a limitation on the scope of the engagement and is often enough to preclude an unmodified opinion. The alternative to representations allowed elsewhere is not permitted."),
("If service organization management refuses to give a written assertion in a SOC 1 engagement, the service auditor should:",
 "Withdraw where law permits", ["Issue a disclaimer of opinion", "Report directly on the controls", "Issue a qualified opinion"],
 "AT-C 320 requires the practitioner to withdraw when management refuses a written assertion, if withdrawal is possible under applicable law or regulation."),
("When the description refers to complementary user entity controls, the service auditor's report states that the auditor:",
 "Has not evaluated those user controls", ["Tested the user controls on a small sample", "Relied on user auditors' testing", "Removed user entities from scope"],
 "The report says the service auditor has not evaluated the suitability of design or operating effectiveness of CUECs, and that the objectives can be met only if they work."),
("Under the carve-out method, the report states that the service auditor's procedures:",
 "Don't extend to the CSOCs", ["Include testing of the CSOCs", "Cover only the user entities' controls", "Rely on the subservice SOC report"],
 "AT-C 320 requires a statement that the auditor's procedures do not extend to complementary subservice organization controls, along with the fact that some objectives depend on them."),
("In a type 2 engagement, significant system changes during the period that management left out of its description should be:",
 "Described in the auditor's report", ["Ignored for the current period", "Tested only after the period ends", "Left for user auditors to find"],
 "AT-C 320 says if significant changes are missing from the description, the service auditor describes them in the report and determines the effect on it."),
("A control relevant to a control objective was replaced halfway through the period. The service auditor should, if possible:",
 "Test the superseded control", ["Test only the new control", "Exclude the earlier months", "Rely on management's description"],
 "AT-C 320 requires testing superseded controls for the part of the period they operated, if possible, and considering the effect on the report if not."),
("May evidence from last year's type 2 engagement reduce the testing needed in this year's type 2 engagement?",
 "No, it is not a basis", ["Yes, if controls didn't change", "Yes, with an updated walkthrough", "Only for automated controls"],
 "AT-C 320 says evidence about controls in prior engagements does not provide a basis for reducing testing, even if supplemented with current-period evidence."),
("The title of a service auditor's report must include the word:",
 "Independent", ["Assurance", "Certified", "Examination"],
 "AT-C 320 requires a title that includes the word independent, for both type 1 and type 2 reports."),
("Under AT-C 320, which item must management's description of its system include, if applicable?",
 "Subservice organization services", ["User entities' financial results", "The auditor's planned sample sizes", "System upgrades planned for next year"],
 "The description criteria include services performed by a subservice organization and whether the carve-out or inclusive method is used. Sample sizes belong to the auditor's tests."),
("A service auditor's report warns that projecting conclusions to future periods is risky because:",
 "Controls may become ineffective", ["Criteria may be withdrawn later", "Users may change their auditors", "The report may be shared widely"],
 "The inherent limitations paragraph notes that controls at a service organization may become ineffective, so evaluations cannot be projected to future periods."),
("When testing controls, the service auditor must combine inquiry with:",
 "Inspection, observation or reperformance", ["Inquiry of several other employees", "Written management representations", "Analytical procedures on outputs"],
 "AT-C 320 requires other procedures such as inspection, observation or reperformance together with inquiry. Inquiry alone, even of several people, is not enough."),
("A service auditor learns that identified deviations resulted from fraud by service organization personnel. The auditor should:",
 "Reassess the risks to its opinions", ["Ignore it if the amount is small", "Notify user entities directly", "Withdraw from the engagement at once"],
 "AT-C 320 requires assessing the risk that the description is not fairly presented and the controls are not suitably designed or operating effectively."),
("In a SOC 2 type 2 report, an exception found when testing a control is shown in the:",
 "Description of tests and results", ["Management's assertion", "System boundaries section", "Separate management letter to the board"],
 "The service auditor's description of tests of controls and results lists each test, the items tested and any exceptions noted."),
("Which must the service auditor have obtained before dating a SOC 1 report?",
 "Management's written assertion", ["User entities' financial statements", "Letters from each user auditor", "Next period's system description"],
 "AT-C 320 dates the report no earlier than when the auditor has sufficient appropriate evidence, including that management prepared the description and provided a written assertion and the documentation was reviewed."),
("Compared with a SOC 2 type 2 report, a SOC 3 report leaves out:",
 "Detailed tests and results", ["The opinion on effectiveness", "Management's assertion", "The period covered"],
 "A SOC 3 report contains an opinion on the operating effectiveness of controls but no detailed description of the tests and their results."),
]
